{'symbol': 'LLY', 'date': '2020-07-30 10:30:00', 'title': 'LILLY REPORTS Q2 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.89', 'text': 'LILLY REPORTS SECOND-QUARTER FINANCIAL RESULTS, RAISES EPS GUIDANCE.Q2 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.89.Q2 REVENUE $5.499 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $5.76 BILLION.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.56 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES FY 2020 EARNINGS PER SHARE $6.48 TO $6.68.SEES FY 2020 REVENUE $23.7 BILLION TO $24.2 BILLION.SECOND-QUARTER 2020 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.55 ON A REPORTED BASIS.LILLY - ESTIMATED NEGATIVE IMPACT OF COVID-19 PANDEMIC ON Q2 REVENUE INCLUDED ABOUT $250 MILLION OF DECREASED CUSTOMER BUYING THAT LARGELY OFFSET Q1 STOCKING.ELI LILLY - CONTINUES TO RAPIDLY ADVANCE DEVELOPMENT OF POTENTIAL THERAPEUTICS FOR TREATMENT OF COVID-19, INCLUDING ANTIBODY THERAPIES AND BARICITINIB.SEES 2020 EPS GUIDANCE RAISED TO BE IN THE RANGE OF $6.48 TO $6.68 ON A REPORTED BASIS AND $7.20 TO $7.40 ON A NON-GAAP BASIS.Q2 ALSO HAD ABOUT $250 MILLION OF LOWER REVENUE RESULTING FROM DELAYED NEW PATIENT PRESCRIPTION TRENDS.CONTINUES TO RAPIDLY ADVANCE DEVELOPMENT OF POTENTIAL THERAPEUTICS FOR TREATING COVID-19, ANTIBODY THERAPIES, BARICITINIB.FOR Q2 OF 2020, WORLDWIDE TALTZ REVENUE INCREASED 12 PERCENT COMPARED WITH Q2 OF 2019, TO $395.2 MILLION.Q2 2020 WORLDWIDE TRULICITY REVENUE WAS $1.230 BILLION, AN INCREASE OF 20 PERCENT COMPARED WITH THE SECOND QUARTER OF 2019.REMAIN CONFIDENT IN OUTLOOK FOR YEAR.EXPECT GROWTH IN NEW PRESCRIPTION VOLUME FOR KEY GROWTH PRODUCTS IN SECOND HALF OF 2020.'}